  "id": "stimulus-generalization",
  "term": "stimulus generalization",
  "definition": "Stimulus generalization is the ability to treat two distinguishable stimuli as similar enough that they lead to the same learned response or consequence. In learning, it describes applying an association learned for one stimulus to a new but related stimulus.",
